  Rendered by the release job with:

      cargo about generate -c docs/about.toml -o <out> docs/third-party-notices.hbs

  The release job prepends a header carrying the tag, the commit and
  SlugAudit's own `Required Notice:` line; this template renders only the
  dependency graph, which is everything `cargo-about` knows about.

  Triple braces (`{{{ }}}`) are deliberate: handlebars HTML-escapes `{{ }}`,
  which would turn every `&`, `"` and `<` in a licence text into an entity.
--}}
THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS AND LICENSES

This list covers every crate `cargo build --release --bin slugaudit` compiles
for x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, with the licence text each crate ships. It is
generated from the release's own `Cargo.lock`, so it describes the dependency
graph the shipped binary was built from — not a scan of the binary itself.

